From: inFAMOUS FoB Recomp contributors
Subject: [PATCH 0015] video: support decoded RSX texture formats, resolve feedback sampling and prevent cutscene composite overwrite

- Whitelist all decoded RSX texture formats (16-bit packed, HILO normal maps, depth, 32-bit floats)
  in d3d12_bind_texture and render_frame prepass to eliminate NULL SRV drops on props and surfaces.
- Snapshot active render target into a scratch feedback copy when sampled as SRV (e.g. refraction/blending
  on glass bottles and props), breaking the D3D12 RTV/SRV concurrent binding hazard.
- Track offscreen draw count in render_frame and bypass composite_present when no offscreen draws occur,
  preserving Bink video cutscenes and 2D UI rendered directly to swapchain backbuffer.
- Add hybrid spin-yield to cellGcmSetWaitFlip loop to reduce guest frame pacing stalls.

